   "installerTest": "Press and hold Menu for 5 seconds to reach the ADVANCED MENU, select System Test, then choose the test type (heat, cool or fan). For heat and cool tests use the controls to turn each equipment stage on; for the fan test toggle the fan on and off. The thermostat clock acts as the test timer and the display shows 'Heat On' / 'Cool On' while the test is running. Source: honeywellhome.com support article 'How do I perform a system test in order to test the stages of equipment?'. Related caution from 33-00231EFS General system information: 'Compressor protection is bypassed during testing. To prevent equipment damage, avoid cycling the compressor quickly.'",
   "factoryReset": "Two documented routes, both official: (a) User-menu route (33-00231EFS 'Reset options', p.24): touch Menu on the home screen, arrow to RESET, touch Select, arrow to the reset option you want, touch Select, then touch Yes to confirm or No to back out. The reset options are Factory reset (back to original factory settings), Schedule reset (back to the default Mon-Fri / Sat-Sun schedule), HomeKit (clears Apple HomeKit device credentials) and Wi-Fi reset (clears the Wi-Fi router credentials). (b) Support-article route (honeywellhome.com 'How Do I Reset My Honeywell Home Device?', T5+/T5/T6 row covering RCHT8610WF, RCHT8612WF, TH6320WF2, TH6220WF2): press and hold Menu, navigate to Reset, then Factory Reset."
