   "Wiring diagrams in the manual: Conventional up to 2H/2C; Conventional w/ PEK; Heat pump up to 4H/2C; Heat pump w/ PEK; Multi-speed 2-pipe fan coil w/ pipe sensor; Multi-speed 2-pipe fan coil w/ Aux Heat; 4-pipe fan coil; 2-wire Heat only (T&T) using Fast-Stat Common-Maker; 2/3-wire Heat only (R,W,G) using Fast-Stat Common-Maker; Two-transformer config (forced-air cooling & radiant heat); 1-wire accessory (ACC+); 2-wire accessory (ACC+/ACC-).",
   "W3 (3-stage furnace) or Y3 (3-stage cooling) wires on the old thermostat mean the system is unsupported as-is; documented workaround is jumpering W2-W3 or Y2-Y3 at the furnace control board (power off first) - ecobee recommends booking a pro for this.",
   "B-only wire (no separate O) goes into O/B; if the system shows both O and separate B wires, or a B wire that is actually the common (C), a pro install is recommended.",
   "Multi-speed fan (multiple G wires) is supported on Premium, Enhanced, ecobee3 lite, SmartThermostat with voice control, and ecobee4 (firmware 4.6.3+)."
