     "notes": "'When configured for O, the reversing valve is energized in Cooling. This will cover most applications. Some manufacturers, such as Rheem or Rhudd, use the B terminal, which would energize in Heating. For three-wire zone hydronic systems set this to 6.' When configured for 2C, second-stage cooling is energized; when configured for 2H, second-stage heating is energized."
