  "wiringNotes": [
   "Single-transformer systems use the factory RH-RC jumper wire (Figure 2). For two-transformer heat/cool systems remove the jumper wire between RH and RC (Figure 3).",
   "There is no GAS/ELECTRIC slide switch on this model - fan control is a menu selection (Configuration Menu item 2): GAS = furnace controls the blower, ELE = thermostat controls the blower. Select ELE if the heating system requires the thermostat to energize the fan.",
   "The rear-view drawing marks an A1 position with the note 'A1 For Damper Control Not Applicable To This Model' - do not attempt to use it on the 1F95-0671.",
   "Power Stealing Switches (two, on the rear of the thermostat) should be left in the On position for most systems; move to Off only if the Power Stealing Assist symptoms listed in power.notes appear.",
   "3-wire SPDT heat-only zone valve wiring uses terminal 6 (closes valve, marked (6) in the figure), W (opens valve, marked (4)), G (blower/circulator), RH (24V hot heat, marked (5)), RC and C.",
   "Comfort Alert II module (or similar system diagnostic module) wires to L, and requires a common connection for diagnostic/malfunction indication.",
   "Electrical rating: mV to 30 VAC NEC Class II 50/60 Hz or DC; hardwire input 20 to 30 VAC; 1.5 A per terminal, 2.5 A maximum all terminals combined."
  ],
  "setup": {
   "access": "Thermostat must be in Heat, Cool or Auto. Press and hold the Menu button for at least 5 seconds - the display shows menu item #1. Press Menu to advance to the next item; press Up or Down to change the option. The menu table has three reference columns (Menu Ref / HP / SS) because item numbers shift depending on whether a heat pump or single/multi-stage system is selected; numbers below are the base Menu Ref column.",
   "keySettings": [
    {
     "setting": "Item 1 - System type",
     "options": "MS 2 (default, multi-stage no heat pump), HP 1 (heat pump, 1 compressor), HP 2 (heat pump, 2-stage or 2-compressor), SS 1 (single stage)",
     "notes": "Must be set before the rest of the menu - several items only appear for certain selections"
    },
    {
     "setting": "Item 2 - Fan control (GAS/ELE)",
     "options": "GAS (default for SS/MS) or ELE (default for HP)",
     "notes": "GAS: furnace controls the blower. ELE: thermostat controls the blower."
    },
    {
     "setting": "Item 5 - Heat cycle rate (CR Heat)",
     "options": "ME (default), SL, FA",
     "notes": "Only appears when MS 2 or SS 1 selected. Differentials: Heat FA 0.4 deg F / ME 0.6 deg F / SL 1.7 deg F"
    },
    {
     "setting": "Item 6 - Heat pump cycle rate (CR Heat Pump)",
     "options": "ME (default), SL, FA",
     "notes": "Only appears when HP 1 or HP 2 selected. Heat Pump FA 0.9 / ME 1.2 / SL 1.7 deg F"
    },
    {
     "setting": "Item 7 - Cool cycle rate (CR Cool) or Aux cycle rate (CR AU)",
     "options": "CR Cool ME (default), SL, FA (SS1/MS2). CR AU FA (default), SL (HP1/HP2)",
     "notes": "Cool FA 0.9 / ME 1.2 / SL 1.7 deg F; Emer (Aux) FA 0.6 / SL 1.7 deg F"
    },
    {
     "setting": "Item 8 - Compressor Lockout (CL)",
     "options": "OFF (default) or CL On",
     "notes": "On makes the thermostat wait 5 minutes between cooling cycles; setpoint flashes for up to 5 minutes during the delay"
    },
    {
     "setting": "Item 12 - Fahrenheit / Celsius",
     "options": "F (default) or C",
     "notes": ""
    },
    {
     "setting": "Item 20 - Remote temperature sensor",
     "options": "Remote OFF (default) / On; then Remote In (default) or Outdoor; then Indoor Loc On (default) or OFF",
     "notes": "Wired sensors F145-1328 (indoor) and F145-1378 (outdoor). Local sensor disable only applies when an indoor remote is enabled."
    },
    {
     "setting": "Item 22 - Keypad Lockout",
     "options": "OFF (default), L (total), P (partial - Up/Down still work), Limit (blocks changing temperature limits); then combination 000 (invalid) or 001-999",
     "notes": "Record the combination. Forgotten code: press and hold the Menu key for 20 seconds to unlock."
    },
    {
     "setting": "Item 25 - Compressor Off (CO) / dual fuel",
     "options": "CO 05 default (disabled), 06 to 50 deg F; then dF (default) or EA; then Cd compressor delay 60 s default, 0-99 s",
     "notes": "Heat pump modes only and requires an enabled outdoor sensor. dF = fossil fuel aux; EA = electric aux (compressor keeps running with aux)."
    },
    {
     "setting": "Item 29 - Reversing valve output",
     "options": "Cool On (o) factory default, or Heat On (b)",
     "notes": "O = changeover relay energized in COOL (majority of heat pumps); B = energized in HEAT"
    },
    {
     "setting": "Item 3 - Cool Savings (CS)",
     "options": "CS 3 default; 0 (disables), 1, 2, 4, 5, 6",
     "notes": "1 = least offset, 6 = most offset"
    },
    {
     "setting": "Item 4 - Energy Management Recovery (E)",
     "options": "On (default) or OFF",
     "notes": "Starts heat ~5 min/deg early (15 min/deg for heat pump); cooling ~15 min/deg. Skipped if configured non-programmable."
    },
    {
     "setting": "Item 9 - System Mode Configuration",
     "options": "Em Heat, Auto, Cool, Off (default set) or Heat Cool Off / Heat Off with Fan icon / Heat Off without Fan icon / Cool Off / Auto Off",
     "notes": "Selects which SYSTEM positions are available, including Auto changeover"
    },
    {
     "setting": "Item 10 - Display light (dL)",
     "options": "dL On (default) or dL OFF",
     "notes": "Continuous backlight only works when C is powered; otherwise momentary on keypress regardless of setting"
    },
    {
     "setting": "Item 11 - Temperature Display Adjustment",
     "options": "4 LO to 4 HI (0 default)",
     "notes": "Adjusts the displayed room temperature up to 4 degrees higher or lower; referenced by this entry's troubleshooting rows"
    }
   ],
   "installerTest": "Check Thermostat Operation section: Fan - turn on power, press FAN to ON (blower starts), press FAN to AUTO (blower stops immediately); skip if there is no G connection. Heating - press SYSTEM to Heat (light a standing pilot first if present), press Up to 1 deg above room temp, heat should run and display shows 'System On' (a flashing setpoint means the 5-minute compressor lockout is active); raise to 3 deg above room temp on MS2/HP1/HP2 and aux heat should run with 'System On +2'; press Down below room temp to stop. Emergency - press SYSTEM to EM, raise setpoint, the heat source on W/E runs and the display shows 'System On' with flashing 'EM'. Cooling - press SYSTEM to Cool and lower the setpoint (do NOT run cooling if outdoor temp is below 50 deg F; do not run the compressor unless crankcase heaters have been on 6 hours and the system has been off at least 5 minutes).",
   "factoryReset": "Two documented operations. (1) Hard reset for a blank/erratic display: remove the wires from terminals R and C (do NOT short them together) and remove the batteries for 2 minutes, then replace wires and batteries. (2) To reset the programming, clock and configuration settings to factory defaults, press the Up or Down and the SYSTEM button simultaneously - the thermostat goes blank and then all display segments appear momentarily. Note: a reset returns the installer configuration menu settings and programming to factory settings, so review the installer menu afterwards."
  },
