  "wiringNotes": [
   "IMPORTANT CORRECTION to the assumed product type: despite the 'WH' suffix commonly read as 'WiFi Humidity' and the product living on a current pro1iaq.com product page, the T955WH install manual is explicit and unambiguous that this is a proprietary 916 MHz RF wireless thermostat (like the older Pro1 wireless zoning line), NOT a WiFi/cloud thermostat. The cover page's own 'Wireless Type Selection' section describes FSK/ASK jumper-selectable 916MHz radio modes, and the Specifications section lists 'Frequency: 916 MHz' with no WiFi/802.11 spec anywhere in the document. There is no app, no SSID setup, no cloud connectivity documented. Treat this as a two-piece 916MHz wall-thermostat + Base Module system, functionally similar to the T755WHO PROsync but using the older FSK/ASK radio scheme and different accessory part numbers (RZ251W/RZ250W or R251W/R250W, plus optional W150W wireless repeater).",
   "Wireless Type Selection: thermostat and Base Module both have an FSK/ASK jumper switch (default FSK); all paired components must be set to the same mode. FSK is the recommended default; ASK is only for legacy components that can't do FSK.",
   "Compatible accessories: RZ251W indoor remote / RZ250W outdoor remote (FSK or ASK capable, also compatible with the Z955W wireless zoning controller), or the older R251W/R250W remotes (ASK only), plus a W150W wireless repeater for range extension.",
   "Range: up to ~100 ft with no obstructions, ~50 ft in typical residential construction; if devices are under 50ft apart and still not communicating, relocate using the included 8ft pigtail before permanently mounting; if over 50ft apart, add a W150W repeater.",
   "If remote (indoor/outdoor) sensors are added to the system, the master (wall) thermostat MUST be hardwired -- battery-only operation is only supported when no remotes are used."
  ],
