  "wiringNotes": [
   "Only one wire per connector on any Nest thermostat; more than one wire in a connector can damage the system and the thermostat. (answer/9250973)",
   "This model has no mechanical wire detector - it relies on what the installer enters in the Google Home app. 'Nest Thermostat doesn't use a mechanical detector. It instead uses the information you input in the Google Home app to determine which wires are connected.' (answer/9244860)",
   "Solid-core copper only, 18 to 22 gauge; stranded wire is not supported. (answer/9244860)",
   "Do not enter jumper wires in the compatibility checker; enter connector labels, not wire colors. (answer/9246656)",
   "Only one wire per connector; do not double up.",
   "Do not carry over jumper wires from the old thermostat - not needed.",
   "Stranded wire and high-voltage systems (120V/240V, thick wires with wire nuts, L1/L2 terminal blocks) are not compatible.",
   "Uses the Google Home app exclusively for setup (this is the first Nest thermostat generation set up only through the Home app rather than the legacy Nest app); the app supplies a photo-based custom wiring diagram.",
   "*OB terminal is shared/multi-purpose - Google's guidance specifically calls out asking the app what's connected if migrating from a prior Nest thermostat that already used *OB."
  ],
